Privacy Policy

Last updated: April 19, 2026

Wojciech Kryg ("Us", "We", or "Our") created the application memolki (the "Application").

IMPORTANT NOTICE: The Application is intended for a general audience, including children of all ages. This privacy policy has been created with the aim of full compliance with the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and other child privacy regulations.

1. Data Collection

The Application is local in nature and does not directly collect any Personal Identifiable Information (PII), such as name, email address, or geographical data (location).

The Application does not require logging in or account creation.

1.A. Data Processed by Third Parties

The Application uses third-party services that process a minimal amount of data to provide advertising, analytics, crash reporting, and transaction services. Because the Application is directed at children, all third-party services are configured to comply with child-directed treatment requirements (COPPA). Ad requests are tagged as child-directed (TAFC), meaning no personalized advertising is served.

These companies may collect the following types of data:

* Device Identifiers: Advertising identifiers or installation identifiers used to recognize the device.
* Transaction Data: Information about in-app purchases (IAP).
* Usage Data: Anonymous app usage events (e.g., screens visited, features used).
* Crash Data: Anonymous technical data about application errors (e.g., stack traces, device model, OS version).

Third parties used in the Application:

1. Google AdMob (Advertising): AdMob, owned by Google, is used to display Rewarded Ads. All ad requests are treated as child-directed (TAFC - Tagged for Child Directed Treatment), meaning AdMob will not use identifiers for ad personalization.
   * Link to Google's Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

2. AdMob Mediation Partners (Advertising): The Application uses AdMob mediation, which allows additional advertising networks to compete to serve non-personalized ads. All mediation partners are configured with child-directed treatment. The following mediation partners may serve ads within the Application:

